  "worked_solution": "The tangential component of acceleration is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{T}=\\frac{v\\cdot a}{||v||}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute the acceleration vector by differentiating the velocity vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t{e}^{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{e}^{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8(t+1){e}^{t},\\,-{e}^{t},\\,0\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute $v\\cdot a$ and $||v||:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot a & =\u27e8t{e}^{t},\\,-{e}^{t},\\,4\u27e9\\cdot \u27e8(t+1){e}^{t},\\,-{e}^{t},\\,0\u27e9 \\\\  & =t(t+1){e}^{2t}+{e}^{2t}+0, \\\\  & =({t}^{2}+t+1){e}^{2t}, \\\\ ||v|| & =\\sqrt{{(t{e}^{t})}^{2}+{(-{e}^{t})}^{2}+{(4)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{2}{e}^{2t}+{e}^{2t}+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({t}^{2}+1){e}^{2t}+16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate tangential component of the acceleration, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{T} & =\\frac{v\\cdot a}{||v||} \\\\  & =\\frac{({t}^{2}+t+1){e}^{2t}}{\\sqrt{({t}^{2}+1){e}^{2t}+16}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
